---
title: Mexican Lasagna
description: Layers of corn tortillas, ground turkey, beans and Monterey Jack, built a day ahead.
tags: [casserole, make-ahead]
course: main
cuisine: Tex-Mex
source:
  name: "America's Test Kitchen: The Make-Ahead Cook"
  url: https://www.amazon.com/Make-Ahead-Cook-Americas-Kitchen/dp/1936493845
adapted: true
servings: 6-8
prep time: 1h15m
cook time: 1h10m
---

= Assemble

Heat the @vegetable oil{2%tsp} in a #Dutch oven{} over medium heat until shimmering.

Add the @scallions{4}(sliced thin), @garlic cloves{4}(minced), @chipotle chiles in adobo sauce{4%tsp}(canned, minced), @salt{1/2%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp} and cook until fragrant (~cook{1%minute}).

Add the @ground turkey{1 1/2%lb}(680 g) and cook, breaking up the meat with a #wooden spoon{}, until no longer pink (~brown{3-5%minutes}).

Stir in the @all-purpose flour{3%tbsp} and cook for ~cook{1%minute}.

Stir in the @chicken broth{2%cup}(473 ml), @green enchilada sauce{1%can}(10 oz), and @pinto beans{1%can}(15 oz, rinsed). Bring to a simmer and cook until the mixture is slightly thickened and the flavors blend (~simmer{10%minutes}).

Turn off the heat, stir in the @frozen corn{300%g}(about 2 cups, thawed) and @fresh cilantro{1/3%cup}(minced) and let cool to room temperature (~cool{30%minutes}).

Brush both sides of the @corn tortillas{18} with the remaining @&vegetable oil{10%tsp}. Stack the tortillas, wrap them in a damp #dish towel{}, and place on a #plate{}. Microwave until warm and pliable (~warm{1%minute}).

Spread 1/3 of the cooled turkey mixture on the bottom of a 13x9 #baking dish{}. Arrange 6 @&corn tortillas{} on top of the filling, overlapping as needed, and sprinkle with @Monterey Jack cheese{113%g}(1 cup, shredded).

Repeat the layer of filling, tortillas, and @&Monterey Jack cheese{113%g} once more.

Spread the remaining filling in the dish. Cut the remaining 6 tortillas into quarters and scatter over the filling. Sprinkle the remaining @&Monterey Jack cheese{113%g} on top.

= To Store

Wrap the dish tightly in #plastic wrap{} and refrigerate for ~chill{24%hours} (or freeze after that).

= To Serve

Adjust the oven rack to the middle position and heat the oven to 400°F (205°C). Unwrap the dish and cover tightly with greased #aluminum foil{}.

Bake the casserole until hot throughout and bubbling around the edges (~bake{30%minutes}).

Remove the foil and continue to bake until the topping is golden brown (~bake{15%minutes}).

Let cool for ~cool{10%minutes}. Sprinkle with the @&fresh cilantro{} and serve.
